# Agent roles

Follow `AGENTS.md` and `docs/AGENT_WORKFLOW.md`. Approved issues proceed directly
to implementation and risk-based checks, then a PR to develop and independent
ChatGPT GitHub PR review. Do not impose a PM → UX → CTO handoff chain.

The read-only prompts in `.cursor/agents/` are available when explicitly requested:

- `product-spec-reviewer`: unresolved problem, scope or acceptance criteria.
- `product-ux-designer`: unresolved interaction choices; no implementation issues.
- `engineering-planner`: significant architecture, migration or test questions.
- `implementation-reviewer`: optional advisory diff review or reusable checklist.

Local advisory review does not replace independent ChatGPT PR review. Never
approve your own implementation as independent. Periodic Product Owner testing
is separate from routine merges; release approval remains human-controlled.
Commit, push and merge only within explicit user authorization.
